<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    PawmodoroWidgetsExtension — privacy manifest.

    An app extension is its own bundle with its own executable, so it needs
    its own manifest; the app's copy at Pawmodoro/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy does
    not reach inside the .appex.

    This target compiles two things: everything in PawmodoroWidgets/, and
    exactly one file borrowed from the app —
    Pawmodoro/LiveActivity/PawmodoroActivityAttributes.swift, named in the
    membership exception in project.pbxproj. Both were audited together.

    Only one required-reason API appears, once:

      1C8F.1  — PawmodoroHomeWidget.swift:61 opens
                UserDefaults(suiteName: "group.com.pawmodoro") to read the
                buddy the app mirrored there, so the widget draws the right
                animal. App Group container, both sides claim the group in
                their entitlements.

    CA92.1 is deliberately NOT declared here. The extension never touches
    UserDefaults.standard — a reason with nothing behind it is a claim this
    app has no business making, even a harmless-looking one.

    The other four categories — file timestamp, system boot time, disk
    space, active keyboards — are absent from this target, the same as in
    the app. No network, no tracking, no collection.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>1C8F.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
